   "note": "A lamp at every intersection corner of the district's drawn streets, in the corner square 1.5 ft inside both curbs (the curb-return corner, between where the two crossings land), on a stone footing; the pictured mid-block lamps at their lots; the rest of every face at about 160 ft, the two sides of a street staggered, on the parkway 0.4 m off the walk, each moved along the parkway clear of an elm, a carriage walk or an alley mouth. A corner where a face meets a curved return (Calumet at 18th) has no corner of its own."
  },
